## Executive Summary & System Overview

The **Virtual Fitting Room Kiosk System** is an in-store hardware-software solution designed for textile and garment retailers. It enables shoppers to visually "try on" garments photorealistically via GPU-accelerated Virtual Try-On (VTON) diffusion models and receive data-backed size recommendations, without needing physical changing rooms or pre-existing 3D garment assets from brands.

### Primary Operational Flow
1. **Interactive Touch Kiosk:** Shopper touches screen, accepts explicit privacy consent.
2. **Edge Vision Pose Guidance:** Real-time MediaPipe vision on the kiosk validates user pose (A-pose, lighting, distance, single person) and auto-captures a high-resolution still.
3. **API & Validation:** Image uploaded securely with session token to FastAPI gateway; server re-validates image before queuing.
4. **Queue & Scheduling:** Redis/Celery dispatches job to an isolated GPU worker pool running PyTorch/Diffusers.
5. **AI Inference & Sizing:** Preprocessing (human parsing, DensePose, garment mask) -> Diffusion VTON generation -> Quality gate paste-back -> Real-time status streamed via WebSocket.
6. **Result & Ephemeral Cleanup:** Photorealistic image and size recommendation rendered on screen. Session terminates, triggering strict 15-minute TTL purge of all body imagery.

