## Latency Budget & Performance Analysis

| Stage | Target Latency Budget | Notes / Dependencies |
| :--- | :---: | :--- |
| **Capture & Client Validation** | 0.3 s | MediaPipe Web Worker stability gate |
| **Upload to Gateway** | 0.5 s | 1080p JPEG over store Wi-Fi/Ethernet |
| **Server Validation & Enqueue** | 0.2 s | FASTApi async check + Redis enqueue |
| **Queue Wait (p50)** | 0.5 s | Sized worker pool |
| **Person & Garment Preprocessing**| 0.8 s | Parsing & DensePose execution |
| **Diffusion Generation** | 3.5 – 6.0 s | FP16 UNet generation |
| **Postprocessing & Quality Gate** | 0.5 s | Paste-back & identity check |
| **Result Delivery & Render** | 0.3 s | Signed URL delivery over WebSocket |
| **Total Latency Budget** | **6.6 s – 9.1 s** | **p50 target < 8s, p95 < 15s** |

> [!NOTE]
> The sub-4 second stretch goal requires heavy UNet distillation, lower working resolution, or TensorRT engine compilation. The document pragmatically advises designing the UX for an 8–10 second expectation with live progress bars and intermediate low-res previews.

