## Security, Privacy & Compliance Architecture

> [!IMPORTANT]
> Full-body imagery and physical measurements constitute **biometric and sensitive personal data** under GDPR, CCPA, and Illinois BIPA.

* **Ephemeral Imagery Lifecycle:** Person stills and intermediate masks are stored in encrypted object storage (MinIO/NVMe) with a **hard 15-minute TTL** and automatic deletion upon session finish.
* **Database Isolation:** PostgreSQL stores zero personal imagery or biometric templates—only session UUIDs, timestamp metadata, and audit logs.
* **Kiosk OS Hardening:** Hardware ports disabled, BIOS password locked, OS shell restricted via Windows Assigned Access / Linux Kiosk mode, full-disk encryption enabled.
* **Network & Device Security:** Kiosks issue mTLS device certificates; secrets kept in vault (never in Electron app bundle); per-kiosk rate limits enforced.

